---

## 11. Metadata Extraction

The parser extracts metadata including:

- File name
- File extension
- File size
- Page count (where applicable)
- Character count
- Upload timestamp
- Content type

---

## 12. Error Handling

| Failure | Behaviour |
|----------|-----------|
| Unsupported format | Reject document |
| Corrupted file | Return parsing error |
| Empty document | Reject ingestion |
| Extraction failure | Log error and stop processing |
| Oversized document | Reject according to platform limits |

---

## 13. Security Considerations

The Document Parser Tool:

- Validates supported file types.
- Rejects malicious or invalid files.
- Enforces maximum file size limits.
- Sanitizes extracted content.
- Logs parsing failures.

---

## 14. Performance Considerations

- Stream large documents where possible.
- Minimize memory usage.
- Support asynchronous parsing.
- Avoid duplicate parsing.
- Process files independently.

